# Messages the file mailer writes in development, and the candidate CVs the file
# CV store writes. Correspondence and other people's documents, and not
# something to commit.
#
# Anchored to the two places they are actually written: the web project, which is
# the content root both options are relative to, and the repository root for
# anything run from there. They were written as bare "mail/" and "cvs/", which
# match a directory of that name at any depth — and because a checkout on a
# case-insensitive filesystem matches these rules without regard to case, "mail/"
# silently swallowed src/JiranisokoTech.Application/Mail,
# src/JiranisokoTech.Infrastructure/Mail and tests/JiranisokoTech.Tests/Mail. The
# mail increment therefore compiled on the machine that wrote it and in no fresh
# clone of it, and nothing said so, because git does not report an ignored file
# as missing. "cvs/" was the same trap with no source folder in it yet.
/mail/
/cvs/
src/JiranisokoTech.Web/mail/
src/JiranisokoTech.Web/cvs/

# Worktrees the agent tooling creates. Not part of the project.
.claude/worktrees/
